# Kling O3 — human gesture vocabulary

## Rule

All **Kling O3 staging and gesture language** uses **human body-part names** (`hand`, `arm`) — not species-specific terms (`flipper`, `paw`, `talon`).

**Keep** parts humans lack an equivalent for: `tail`, `shell`, `horns`, `beak` (on birds), `fur`, `feathers`, etc.

**Exception:** legacy **bird / Chipper** beats must **not** say `hand` — wing vocabulary only (see `CHIPPER_VIDEO_RELIABILITY_SPEC_v1.md`).

## Why

Kling animates micro-gestures from text; human terms produce reliable waves/shrugs/points. `@Image1` Element still locks species appearance.

## Enforcement (code — do not rely on prompts alone)

| Layer | Location |
|---|---|
| Plan normalize | `beat_extract_policy.humanize_kling_body_parts()` in `normalize_plan_row` |
| Author postprocess | `postprocess_kling_author_row` |
| Approve heal | `heal_segment_dialogue_fields` |
| Submit gate | `prepare_kling_o3_prompt_for_submit` |
| Sidecar migrate v3 | `_migrate_sidecar` → heals existing beats without re-approve |

## Authoring

- Planner SKILL + EVENT2 gold: hand not flipper/paw
- `kling_staging_policy_block()`: hand flutter, not wing-flutter (except birds)
